   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The double negative",
     "texto": [
      "**Ne** goes before the conjugated verb and the negative word usually comes after: **Je ne travaille plus**, **Je ne fais rien**, **Je ne parle à personne**. In the passé composé, **ne** goes before the auxiliary and **rien/personne** after: **Je n'ai rien mangé**, **Je n'ai vu personne**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "When «rien» or «personne» is the subject",
     "texto": [
      "They can also go before the verb: **Personne ne vient** (nobody comes), **Rien ne va** (nothing is going well). The position depends on their function: as a subject they go first; as an object they usually go after the verb or the auxiliary."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
